   "text": "Greer said that in eight years of negotiating with the Chinese, export controls always came up in meetings. He described export controls as protecting critical U.S. technology and as a national-security matter, not something that applies only to China. He also said the baseline for export controls can be adjusted as technology advances and access improves.",
